# Authenticates a Tenant and issues an access token (account/API-key
# management only — never valid on the log endpoints) plus a refresh token.

### Happy path
POST http://localhost:8080/tenants/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@example.com",
  "password": "correct-horse-battery-staple"
}

### Wrong password — expect 401, same message as an unknown email
POST http://localhost:8080/tenants/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "customer@example.com",
  "password": "totally-wrong-password"
}

### Unknown email — expect 401 with the identical message (no disclosure)
POST http://localhost:8080/tenants/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nobody@example.com",
  "password": "correct-horse-battery-staple"
}
